exports[`renderPretty > renders the incident with code frame, matrix, context, why, fix and docs 1`] = `
"
── .github/workflows/tests.yml ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── 1 error

✖  ERROR  FP401 empty-binding-for-matrix-combo
  Input "config" for .github/workflows/run-suite.yml is empty in 1 of 3 matrix combinations —
  matrix.config is not defined there

  ▶ .github/workflows/tests.yml:23:19
    21 │       suite: \${{ inputs.suite }}
    22 │       variant: \${{ matrix.name }}
    23 │       config: \${{ matrix.config }}
       │                   ━━━━━━━━━━━━━

  matrix  { name: windows }
  context ├─ .github/workflows/pipeline.yml:9:11   jobs.tests calls .github/workflows/tests.yml
          ├─ .github/workflows/tests.yml:18:13     this include entry has no \`config\`
          ├─ .github/workflows/run-suite.yml:11:7  receives the empty value: input "config"
          └─ .github/workflows/run-suite.yml:17:9  this condition reads "config", so the legs with an empty value take the other branch
  why     GitHub evaluates a missing matrix key to an empty string — no error, no warning. The
          affected matrix leg runs with an empty input, so the callee may skip its real work
          (e.g. a test configuration) while the run stays green.
  fix     Set \`config\` in every combination, or use a fallback: \`\${{ matrix.config ||
          '<default>' }}\`.
  docs    https://ciatlas.github.io/flowpact/docs/rules/fp401

╭─ Summary ──────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
